diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-kernel-zest-swap-fault-stats b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-kernel-zest-swap-fault-stats
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a6f3b073b8cd8721fd066a6a74cf4be995aa7795
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-kernel-zest-swap-fault-stats
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+What:		/sys/kernel/zest/swap_fault_stats
+Date:		2026-09-05
+Contact:	Android memory management maintainers
+Description:
+		Read-only key/value counters for logical swap faults across all
+		swap devices. A fault that returns VM_FAULT_RETRY is counted once;
+		the first swap-cache lookup determines whether it is a hit or miss.
+
+		The output is:
+
+		  page_faults: <u64>
+		  swap_cache_hits: <u64>
+		  swap_cache_misses: <u64>
+		  async_retry_pending: <u64>
+		  async_retry_overflow: <u64>
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/zest/swap_fault_stats_reset
+Date:		2026-09-05
+Contact:	Android memory management maintainers
+Description:
+		Write 1, y, or true to reset all counters and discard pending
+		retry associations. Generation fencing prevents an in-flight fault
+		from publishing an association created before the reset. Writing
+		0 or false is a no-op; invalid boolean values are rejected with
+		-EINVAL.
